  {
   "k": "1g2q3nq",
   "en": "⟦0⟧ are special, releasable puppet states which can only be formed by the ⟦1⟧ in controlled enemy territory, following the completion of the focus ⟦2⟧. They are created using decisions after conquering the relevant territory. Additional puppet states become available after completing the focuses ⟦3⟧, ⟦4⟧ and ⟦5⟧. All of the puppet states are ⟦6⟧, with the exception of ⟦7⟧, which is a ⟦8⟧, but for the purposes of this article will sometimes be called a Reichskommissariat. The Reichskommissariats do not have core states, but are nonetheless designed to limit the amount of ⟦9⟧ occupied territory in order to reduce the negative effects of the ⟦10⟧ national spirit. Almost all territory in the game can be made into Reichskommissariats, notable exceptions being ⟦11⟧, ⟦12⟧, ⟦13⟧, ⟦14⟧, ⟦15⟧, ⟦16⟧, ⟦17⟧, ⟦18⟧, ⟦19⟧, Crete, the Bosporus Strait, and the Suez Canal. The ⟦20⟧ starts as an playable country in 1939, but will normally be created by ⟦21⟧ if it annexes ⟦22⟧ via an event during historical playthroughs.",
   "frags": 23
